WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.553
Step six adds the QUIC rule on the pilot
device, Learn's Windows Firewall command;

2
00:00:05.553 --> 00:00:10.138
in production the same rule goes
out through Intune, piloted first.

3
00:00:10.138 --> 00:00:14.457
Steps seven and eight need a T L
S inspection certificate created,

4
00:00:14.457 --> 00:00:17.017
enabled and trusted on the test device,

5
00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:22.217
and a pilot T L S policy linked to the
pilot security profile, never the baseline,

6
00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:24.217
as the guide's Step 9 describes,

7
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:27.737
with the privacy officer's
approval of the test scope.

8
00:00:27.737 --> 00:00:32.691
Step seven checks the issuer of an
inspected site in the browser's certificate

9
00:00:32.691 --> 00:00:37.263
viewer: Microsoft Global Secure Access
Intermediate, or your test chain.

10
00:00:37.263 --> 00:00:42.857
Step eight reads the T L S outcomes: T L
S action reads bypassed or intercepted,

11
00:00:42.857 --> 00:00:46.675
and the failure share should
stay under one percent.

12
00:00:46.675 --> 00:00:49.787
Step nine exports the
profiles and policies.

13
00:00:49.787 --> 00:00:51.138
Keep it all in place.

14
00:00:51.138 --> 00:00:55.097
Module 6 removes it, and the
T L S policy in Learn's order:

15
00:00:55.097 --> 00:00:59.830
the link from the profile, then
the policy, then the certificate.
